2026-10-25T00:10:00Z  ROOT     The live Explore envelope is the content_item shape: feeds[] carry feed_id/feed_title; items[] carry {content_id, content_type, content_item}; the first feed's six items are content_type "shortcut" (shortcut_schema: name/image_url/redirect_url); the second feed's items are content_type "generic_feed" whose content_item is ITSELF a feed (feed_id/feed_title/items) and whose items are content_type "clip" with song_schema payloads. SunoExploreService::parsePage read feed["id"]/feed["title"] and looked for a clip at the top of each item, so every feed parsed as label "Explore" with zero clips -- a 200 behind an empty page.
2026-10-25T00:10:00Z  CHANGE   src/suno/SunoExploreService.cpp: feedLabel prefers feed_title; parsePage delegates to a new appendFeed() that resolves the feed id from feed_id/id/identifier, unwraps content_item (plus the legacy item/clip_schema/clip keys), republishes a nested feed as its own section (depth <= 2), skips a container feed whose only content was nested sections, and drops shortcut/shortcut_schema entries before ClipParser sees them (a tile has an id, so the tolerant parse would have produced a card with no artist or duration). parseClipEntry now also requires a non-empty id.
